course: dictionary
lesson: 6666
title: Oak: a tree and its wood
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An oak is a big tree with hard wood that can live for hundreds of years. The word oak can name the tree, or the strong wood the tree gives us. It can also describe something, as in a table made of oak.
explain: Read this: «Grey squirrels bury nuts in many separate spots, and the acorns they and jays forget can grow into new oak trees.» Acorns are the nuts of an oak. The context tells you a forgotten acorn can grow into a new oak tree, so here oak means the tree.
explain: Oak also appears in a saying: «great oaks from little acorns grow». Great oaks are big trees and little acorns are tiny nuts. The saying means big things often start small, so you can work out its meaning from the words around it.
fact: An oak is a big tree with hard wood that can live for hundreds of years.
fact: Acorns are the nuts of an oak tree.
fact: Oak is also the strong wood from the tree, used for furniture and floors.
fact: In autumn, oaks lose their leaves, and many insects and birds live in an oak.
exercise: In «a great old oak in the forest», what is an oak? | A small plant with soft stems | A pile of cut logs | *A big, old tree | A kind of bird that lives in the forest
exercise: Jayden's new table is made of oak. What does oak mean here? | *The strong wood from the oak tree | A nut that drops in autumn | A kind of bird | A tree in the forest
exercise: In «great oaks from little acorns grow», which word means the small nut from an oak? | *acorns | grow | great | oaks
test: «The acorns they forget can grow into new oak trees.» What are the nuts of an oak called? | Berries | Cones | Conkers | *Acorns
test: In autumn, what happens to the leaves of an oak? | They glow in the dark | They turn into acorns | *They fall off | They grow bigger
exam: What does the saying «great oaks from little acorns grow» mean? | Trees are only grown by people | Acorns are too big to eat | Oaks never grow very tall | *Big things often start small
